---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { getDirectory, formatLongDate } from '../lib/load';

const directory = getDirectory();
const checked = formatLongDate(directory.checkedOn);
---

<Layout
  title="How listings work"
  description="How the Charlotte church directory checks listings, and what is not collected yet."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="How listings work"
    lede="This is a Charlotte pilot. The public pages are built from churches that were checked, plus any submission a reviewer has approved."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'How listings work' }]}
  />
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 space-y-6 text-gray-700">
    <section class="callout">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-gray-900">What "checked" means</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">For the seed set, someone opened the church's own website, copied a short quote (usually the service time), saved the link, and recorded the date. The latest check in this file is {checked || 'recorded on the listing'}.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card p-5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">What you can filter on</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Denomination family, the specific body inside that family, language, city or ZIP, and service time. Those are the details the seed file actually holds.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card p-5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">What is not collected yet</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Kids and youth, worship style, theology, young adults, LGBTQ stance, and outreach have a place in the database and are empty. They will not show up as filters until a listing says so in its own words and a reviewer approves it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card p-5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">Submissions and edits</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">The public forms only create a review row. Approving that row is what creates or updates a church. Rejecting it leaves the public list alone. Churches are not deleted. A closed church stays in the database and can be hidden from the public pages.</p>
    </section>
    <p>
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/submit">Submit a church</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary ml-2" href="/suggest-edit">Suggest an edit</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
